<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Røros</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Roros</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Røros is a mining town in the mountains of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, in Trøndelag. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">Copper</a> was mined there from 1644 until 1977, making the works one of the main sources of revenue for Denmark-Norway. The town's wooden houses and smelting landscape survive largely intact and were listed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 1980.</p></div>
